# The rollback gate, run against the database the agent-operations
# scenario left behind: one monitor really executed by two probes.
# commit b88893a, 2026-08-02T12:48:18Z

=== 1. read-only inventory ===
npm notice run vigil@1.14.0 npx
npm notice run 'tsx' scripts/probe-downgrade.ts
1 monitor is executed by remote probes.

  Ops
    ops-target                         2 named probes     majority  min 1  every 30s  up

After a rollback to 1.13.0 every one of these is checked from the
controller instead, at the same interval, under the same name. Nothing
fails and nothing alerts. What is gone is the agreement between
vantage points.

Before rolling back, choose one:
  --convert      set these monitors back to local execution now, so the
                 rollback changes nothing that has not already changed
  --pause        pause them, so a single-vantage check does not quietly
                 stand in for a quorum
  --acknowledge  keep them as they are and accept that the rollback
                 returns them to local execution
exit: 0

it changed nothing:
  policies still remote:   1
  monitors still unpaused: 1

=== 2. the gate refuses an undecided rollback ===
npm notice run vigil@1.14.0 npx
npm notice run 'tsx' scripts/probe-downgrade.ts --check
1 monitor is executed by remote probes.

  Ops
    ops-target                         2 named probes     majority  min 1  every 30s  up

After a rollback to 1.13.0 every one of these is checked from the
controller instead, at the same interval, under the same name. Nothing
fails and nothing alerts. What is gone is the agreement between
vantage points.

Refusing: no convert, pause or acknowledgement has been recorded since
the policies were last changed. Run this with --convert, --pause or
--acknowledge, then roll back.
exit: 1

=== 3. acknowledging is a decision, and it is recorded ===
npm notice run vigil@1.14.0 npx
npm notice run 'tsx' scripts/probe-downgrade.ts --acknowledge
acknowledged for 1 monitor(s). Recorded in the audit log, and
--check will pass until a policy is changed again.
exit: 0
               action                | actor_id |    monitors    
-------------------------------------+----------+----------------
 probe_policy.downgrade_acknowledged | (none)   | ["ops-target"]
(1 row)

=== 4. and now the gate passes ===
npm notice run vigil@1.14.0 npx
npm notice run 'tsx' scripts/probe-downgrade.ts --check
1 monitor(s) on probes, and a decision is recorded; safe to roll back
exit: 0
